// String-mutation regression fixture for std.mutation. Three string
// literals in the code below: name (tested, killed), motto (untested,
// survives), and help, whose body holds an arithmetic operator inside a
// string that the operator mutators MUST skip. No code-level arithmetic
// operators exist, so every mutant is a string mutant: one killed, two
// survived. (This comment avoids quote characters on purpose, so the
// mutator sees only the three real literals below.)
exports(name, motto, help)

name() -> string { return "alice" }

motto() -> string { return "untested" }

help() -> string { return "a + b" }
